    "body": "`experimental_fn` / `experimental_cls` decide whether an experimental API has reached its end of life by comparing only the *minor* component of the version:\n\n```python\nPkgVersion(introduced_with_version).minor + max_lifetime < PkgVersion(mcore_version).minor\n```\n\nOnce mcore crosses a major boundary and the minor version resets to 0, this comparison can never fire again, so expired experimental APIs silently stop being flagged. For example an API introduced at `0.19.0` with a lifetime of 1 minor version is no longer reported once the package version becomes `1.0.0` (`19 + 1 < 0` is false forever).\n\nThis PR compares the `(major, minor)` pair instead, which keeps the check working across major bumps, and adds regression tests for the major-boundary case.\n\nLocal results: `pytest tests/unit_tests/test_utils.py -k \"eol or experimental\"` — the new tests fail on current main (no exception raised for the major-bump case) and pass with the fix; the rest of `test_utils.py` is unaffected.\n\nNote: I drafted this change with AI assistance; I reviewed and tested it myself.\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
